<title>USA: High cotton prices trigger import quota - USDA.</title>
<headline>High cotton prices trigger import quota - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>High cotton prices triggered another special quota permitting entry of 44,983,440 kilograms (99,171,591 lbs), U.S. Agriculture Department said Thursday.</p>
<p>The quota, being established as of Jan 4, applies to cotton purchased no later than April 3, 1997, and entering the United States no later than July 2, 1997.</p>
<p>The quota amount is for June through August this year.</p>
